Z||000000||Mattyman||12-28-2001||11:07 PM||||My friends and I always have fun breaking things and finding funny things to do with anything from phones to wheelchairs.  We have broken many computer keyboards, one was run over by the Astro Van while spinning tire on ice which launched it about 50 yards.  We have broken an organ and had fun hitting it with sledgehammers and metal pipes. We threw a computer monitor off of the roof of my house, threw a bowling ball through an old tv and alot of other things.  Its always fun to break old junk.  Well we have another old small tv and we dont have any idea of how we should break it.  So if anyone has any suggestions it would be appreciated. Ha Ha  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>You gotta stand for Something or your gonna fall for everything.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Sootah||12-28-2001||11:19 PM||||Get in a FWD car, find some food trays (like the ones at McDonalds, etc) set the trays in front of the rear wheels, drive onto the trays, pull the parking break, then drive. Doughnuts in the summer (or just a dry parkinglot).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__tig_sig2.gif">           <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Don't sweat the petty things, and don't pet the sweaty things</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AOL IM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||14
